\title{usRds: Load, Label and Analyze United States Renal Data System Files}
\description{
\if{html}{\figure{logo.png}{options: style='float: right' alt='logo' width='120'}}

Load, label and analyze files from the United States Renal Data System (USRDS), the national data system on chronic kidney disease and end-stage kidney disease in the United States. Users supply USRDS files they have obtained, in 'SAS', comma-separated values (CSV) or 'Parquet' format; the package finds them, chooses one file for each file name and year, and reads them with upper-case column names. Variables and values can be labelled from the appendices of the USRDS Researcher's Guide. Medicare claims can be extracted by diagnosis, procedure and provider specialty codes, and used to date diagnoses, build cohorts, and compute claim costs with daily proration and medical care inflation adjustment.
}
